# ContextForge integration

This project uses [ContextForge](./README.md) — a deterministic pipeline that produces curated context artifacts to save tokens during AI-assisted development.

## Before suggesting code changes

1. Check if `.contextforge/context-pack.json` exists.
2. If yes, those files are the **primary context** for the current task. Prefer them over reading the entire codebase.
3. Use `.contextforge/graph.json` to understand which files depend on the ones being modified.

## When artifacts are missing or stale

Suggest running this pipeline (deterministic, no LLM, < 30 s):

```bash
pnpm forge scan       # Index files with BLAKE3 hashes
pnpm forge graph      # Build dependency graph (tree-sitter)
pnpm forge context "<task description>"  # PageRank + budget pack
```

## When generating specs

`forge spec <change-id>` always emits OpenSpec format at `openspec/changes/<id>/`.
Reference these files when working on a tracked change.

## When committing

Run `pnpm forge implement --check` before committing changes — validates the diff against guardrails (allowed files, max LOC delta, forbidden paths).

## Token savings observed

Real measurement on this repo: **90.3 % savings** vs full repo dump (11 700 vs 121 000 tokens).
